{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והתנחלתם", :translit "u'hitnachaltem", :gloss "and you shall take possession"} {:he "הכא ואידך גבי עבד", :translit "ka v'idach gabei eved", :gloss "here and the other concerning a slave"} {:he "דעבד איתקש לקרקעות", :translit "d'eved itqesh le'karka'ot", :gloss "which a slave is likened to lands"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והתנחלתם"]}], :frame {:text "The verb והתנחלתם appears twice in the Torah: here in Numbers 33:54 regarding possession of land and in Leviticus 25:46 regarding acquisition of slaves. The hermeneutical principle of gezeirah shavah links topics through shared rare terminology, and the Mishnah applies the land-slave analogy to the law of yovel: just as land reverts at the Jubilee, so Canaanite slaves go free (Kiddushin 15a).", :sources ["Leviticus 25:46" "Kiddushin 15a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והתנחלתם", :translit "u'hitnachaltem", :gloss "and you shall take possession"} {:he "נחלה", :translit "nachalah", :gloss "inheritance"} {:he "כל א' הי\"ל בד'", :translit "kol alef yud-lamed be'dalet", :gloss "each alef yud-lamed in dalet"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "א'", :b "ד'"} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["נחלה"]}], :frame {:text "The verse Numbers 33:54 contains four forms of the root נחלה, corresponding to four categories of Eretz Yisrael terrain — mountain, valley (Numbers 33:54 uses הר and מישור), lowland (shefelah, e.g. Deuteronomy 1:7), and seacoast (e.g. Joshua 11:2). The verse opens with והתנחלתם and closes with לנחלה, teaching that wherever the lot falls, the allocation is binding even when parcels are distant.", :sources ["Numbers 33:54" "Deuteronomy 1:7" "Joshua 11:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והתנחלתם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "והתנחלתם", :refs ["Leviticus 25:46" "Numbers 33:54"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "א'", :a-value 1, :b "ד'", :b-value 4, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {